<!-- BEGIN claude-mindmap -->
## Live architecture mind map

Keep a running Excalidraw mind map of the current project's architecture in the side
panel, using the `mindmap` skill.

Invoke it **at architectural milestones** — when the shape of the system in my head
changed, not on every turn:

- I finished exploring a subsystem and now understand how its pieces connect
- We agreed on a plan spanning more than one module
- A module, route group, service, table, or layer was added, removed, or renamed
- A refactor changed which layer talks to which
- I found a connection that contradicts what the map currently shows

Do **not** invoke it for single-file edits, bug fixes inside one function, test runs,
formatting, dependency bumps, or questions answered from memory. If the map would come
out identical to the last render, skip it silently.

Drawing the map never interrupts the task: draw, say at most one sentence, continue. The
user can force a render any time with `/map`.

If the Excalidraw MCP tools are unavailable in a session, skip the map entirely and don't
mention it.
<!-- END claude-mindmap -->
